+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry owns input validation so every executor receives data checked against the same JSON Schema sent to the model.
+
+## Registry behavior
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates each input against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs; invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failure and does not invoke the executor ([validated by: rejects missing and wrong-typed fields before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- Valid input preserves unlisted properties and reaches the executor unchanged ([validated by: passes valid input with extra properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- A function-valued tool definition is resolved for each execution, and each input is checked against the schema resolved for that call ([validated by: checks each call against its current function-resolved schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L50)).
+- An invalid static schema fails during registration and identifies the tool ([validated by: rejects invalid schemas at registration and preserves unknown-tool errors](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L78)).
+- Invalid tool input returns its validation result to the model, allowing a corrected tool call to proceed in a later round ([validated by: lets the model correct a rejected tool call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
